Notification sounds
===================

Enable these under Settings > Notifications, with "Sound files instead of
beep" and this folder selected. Each file is played when the matching
notification fires; the events are the checkboxes on that same tab.

    MyCall.wav      your callsign appeared in a decode
    DXCC.wav        new DXCC entity
    Grid.wav        new grid square
    CQZone.wav      new CQ zone
    ITUZone.wav     new ITU zone
    NewCall.wav     new callsign
    Wanted.wav      a call, prefix, grid or country from your wanted lists
    Prefix.wav      new prefix

Any file that is missing falls back to the system bell, so you can delete
the ones you do not want and keep the rest. Files are plain WAV; the ones
shipped here are 16-bit mono at 48 kHz.

Prefix.wav is not shipped, so new-prefix notifications ring the bell until
you add one. NewCall.wav is WSJT-X's DXcall.wav under a new name, so the
wording may not match the event exactly - replace it if it bothers you.

The other files come from the WSJT-X project (GPL, same licence as JTDX).
